# bix-51-q1 — Logit(PR ~ Age), predicted P at Age = 65

## Analysis set (data/data.xlsx :: Sheet1)
- Raw read 121x12 -> dropped rows with NaN `Sequence number` (blank rows + trailing row holding only whitespace in `Age`) -> **n = 80**, `Sequence number` = 1..80 contiguous, no duplicates.
- `Age` numeric cast: 0 missing, range **40–75**, mean 58.54 (SD 10.46); **5 patients exactly age 65** (1 PR, 4 non-PR).
- Outcome: `Efficacy == 'PR'` -> y = 1 (**41 events**); SD (17) + PD (22) -> y = 0 (**39 non-events**); unconditional PR rate 0.5125.
- `Groups` (1 = 41, 2 = 39) perfectly cross-tabs with Efficacy (Group1 all PR; Group2 all SD/PD) -> kept OUT of the model (age is the only predictor; adding it gives complete separation).

## Model (statsmodels Logit, MLE, intercept, raw years)
logit P(PR) = **4.4466 (SE 1.4513)** + (**−0.074954**, SE 0.024351) × Age
- OR per year = 0.9278 (Age 95% CI −0.1227 to −0.0272; p = 0.0021)
- llf −50.071, llf(null) −55.427, LR p = 0.00106, McFadden pseudo-R² = 0.0966, AIC 104.14, converged = True
- Manual IRLS/Newton re-fit reproduces betas to 8.9e-16 (sklearn unavailable offline; MLE independently verified)
- Standardised-age refit gives identical p(65) (difference < 1e-9)

## PRIMARY ANSWER — Age = 65
linear predictor = −0.425439 → **p̂ = 0.3952** (39.52 %)
- delta-method SE 0.0678, 95 % CI **0.2624 – 0.5280**
- profile-likelihood 95 % CI **0.2679 – 0.5287**
- statsmodels `get_prediction` cross-check: p 0.3952, SE 0.0678, CI 0.2727 – 0.5325

## Diagnostics (do not alter the estimate)
- mean fitted 0.5125 = observed 0.5125 (intercept-calibrated); predicted range 0.236–0.810
- ROC AUC 0.701; Hosmer–Lemeshow χ²(3) ≈ 0.31 (p ≈ 0.96) -> no evidence of miscalibration
- Empirical reference at age 65: 1/5 = 0.20 PR (n too small to be a usable estimate)

## Sensitivity
- **SD excluded (PR vs PD only, n = 63):** logit = 5.329 − 0.0801·Age → p(65) = **0.5306** (95 % CI 0.373–0.688); differs from primary by **0.135**. Primary answer keeps SD as non-PR.
- **Group-1-only subset (n = 41):** all PR -> outcome constant, complete separation, logistic model not identifiable; documented as a note, no coefficients reported.
